{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>A man, a man.</b> Rashi explained: to teach you that Cutheans vow vows and freewill offerings like Israel. And if you ask: let it be derived from what is written, ״ומיד בן נכר לא תקריבו מכל אלה״ — which implies: these you shall not offer, but unblemished ones you may offer! One may answer: were it not for ״איש איש״, I might have said that gentile nations are altogether included in ״לא תקריבו״, and that one who offers from them unblemished animals transgresses a negative commandment, and blemished ones a negative commandment and a positive commandment. Another resolution: were it not for ״איש איש״, I might have said that Cutheans may offer unblemished animals, even sin-offerings and guilt-offerings. Therefore it says ״איש איש״ — ״for all their vows and for all their freewill offerings״: only vows and freewill offerings may Cutheans offer, but sin-offerings and guilt-offerings, no."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:21.905183596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}